{# The initialiser of one `<data>` in the form the engine policy's `defineData` takes it: the lowered
   `expr`, the inline text read in the order of W3C SCXML B.2 (XML becomes its DOM through the
   library's `_scxml_parse_xml`, an expression its value) with the string it spells as the last
   reading, or none. The text of a `<data src>` (W3C SCXML 5.3.1) is read when the machine is
   generated, through `read_data_src` like the C11 and Python backends, and is then inline text: the
   machine carries no path and opens no file. Written where the document's data is declared at load
   (`script_engine.swift.jinja2`) and where a state with late binding declares its own on its first
   entry (`entry_exit_actions.swift.jinja2`), so the two cannot read one `<data>` two ways.
   `base_path` is the model's `scxml_base_path`, which a macro cannot see for itself.

   It lives beside the Swift templates and not in the shared `_macros/`: the directory is the C++
   backend's by the ownership rule (`Language::owns_template`), so an expression site written there
   would be counted as C++'s. #}
{% macro data_source(var, base_path) -%}
{%- set content = (var.src | read_data_src(base_path)) if var.src else var.content -%}
{%- if var.expr -%}as: "{{ var.expr | to_lua_expr | escape_swift }}"
{%- elif content | data_content_is_xml -%}as: "_scxml_parse_xml(\"{{ content | escape_lua | escape_swift }}\")", orText: "{{ content | normalize_ws | escape_swift }}"
{%- elif content -%}as: "{{ content | to_lua_data_content | escape_swift }}", orText: "{{ content | normalize_ws | escape_swift }}"
{%- else -%}as: nil
{%- endif -%}
{%- endmacro %}
